  "notes": [
    "CT-HYP-6: one Week in the import is one rotation (Days 1 to 3), then a rest day, so the 6 Weeks run about 24 calendar days. Offered only to lifters with 5 or more available days.",
    "CT-HYP-1: reps and RIR change every 2 rotations: 13-15 at RIR 3, then 10-12 at RIR 2, then 5-6 at RIR 0, where free-weight compounds stop at RIR 1 (CT-HYP-3, A-7).",
    "A Nordic curl is a common lower-day choice; at 13 to 15 reps a leg curl fits the phase, with the Nordic curl kept as an alternative. The GHD sit-up is written as Sit Up.",
    "P-7: rear delts, laterals and flyes take 2 sets each so shoulders stay at or under 11 fractional sets on the push day.",
    "CT-HYP-4: name 2 to 4 priority muscles from the lifter's answers in program.priority_muscles; P-3 holds them to 10-20 sets a week.",
    "CT-PT-2: each day opens with the mobility block for its pattern: 5 min rower or bike, three 1-set drills, then Shoulder Big 3 1 x 15 each."
  ]
